-- title:
--   Finite free algebras over (p)-adically complete rings
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal{O}$ be a commutative ring and $p$ a natural number, and suppose $\mathcal{O}$ is adically complete with respect to the ideal generated by the image of $p$ in $\mathcal{O}$, that is, $\mathcal{O}$ is both Hausdorff and precomplete for the $(p)$-adic filtration in Mathlib's sense. Let $R$ be a commutative ring equipped with an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra structure, and assume that $R$ is finite and free as an $\mathcal{O}$-module. The conclusion is that $R$ is adically complete for the ideal of $R$ generated by the image of $p$ in $R$: the canonical map from $R$ to the $(pR)$-adic completion $\varprojlim_n R/p^nR$ is injective (Hausdorff) and every $(pR)$-adically Cauchy sequence in $R$ has a limit (precomplete). Note that the ideal in the hypothesis is an ideal of $\mathcal{O}$ and the one in the conclusion is the corresponding ideal of $R$, so the statement simultaneously transports completeness along the algebra map and identifies the two filtrations; no rank, Noetherianity or primality assumption on $p$ is imposed.
--
--   This is the standard fact that a module-finite free algebra over an $I$-adically complete ring is complete for the extended ideal, specialised to the principal ideal generated by an integer $p$. It serves to discharge $p$-adic completeness hypotheses on auxiliary rings built from a complete coefficient ring $\mathcal{O}$, and is invoked in the formal-étaleness and base-change statements over $\mathbb{Z}/p$ that occur further on.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_IsAdicComplete_of_module_finite_free_span_natCast.lean

